# NOTHING for /blog here. The blog is now served AT onealgorithm.com/blog by the
# oa-blog-debrand worker, which proxies Ghost (url=https://onealgorithm.com/blog).
#
# A rule here would fight that route and win intermittently: while both existed,
# /blog/ and the post served correctly but /blog/sitemap.xml got 301'd to a
# subdomain that no longer serves a root, so it 404'd. Leave this gap alone.

# The careers page has moved to the blog, where jobs are now published.
#
# A 301 rather than a 404 because /careers was the single highest-traffic page
# on this site in search — it drew more impressions than any commercial page,
# and roughly a fifth of LinkedIn page views went to the jobs tab. Letting it
# 404 would discard all of that accrued signal and dead-end every visitor who
# arrives from an existing search result.
#
# Target the careers TAG, not the blog homepage. Someone arriving on /careers
# wants the jobs, and the homepage buries them among every other post — it sent
# candidates to a subscribe box and left them to hunt. The tag page lists every
# post tagged `careers` and needs no maintenance as roles open and close, which
# a link straight to one job post would.
#
# ⛔ Changed 2026-09-14 to the careers PAGE. The oa-blog-debrand worker sends
# X-Robots-Tag: noindex on every tag archive, so this redirect handed the
# site's highest-traffic URL to a page Google is told not to index ("redirect
# to noindex" in Search Console), and Semrush flagged that tag page as 22-word
# thin content. /blog/careers/ is the full 565-word listing the footer already
# links. If roles multiply, make that page list them rather than un-noindexing
# a tag archive.
/careers     /blog/careers/    301
/careers/*   /blog/careers/    301

# /about-us was the old URL for the about page and Google still surfaces it —
# it was returning a 404 to anyone who clicked that result. A 301 keeps the
# accrued signal and, more importantly, stops sending a real visitor to a dead
# end from a search result the company did not choose to have.
/about-us     /about    301
/about-us/*   /about    301

# The pre-redesign services URL still sits in the brand SERP and 404s — Google
# holds signal for it (audit 2026-08-31). Both slash forms, to the live hub.
/our-services  /services  301
/our-services/  /services  301

